      "writtenOn": "2026-06-04T12:52:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Tristan! This is good feedback! I have updated the spec with a Security section.\n\nRegarding `get_file`, in openstacksdk\u0027s `create_stack(template\u003d\u003cstring\u003e)` the `files` parameter defaults to empty. Would have to use helper `read_env_and_templates(template_file\u003d\u003cpath\u003e)` to load and pass file content to the service. So I do not think that leak would have been possible. Nevertheless I updated the spec to do parsing when loading config and raise an error early. Block any `get_file` use in template at config load!\n\nI also identified a couple of other things, `deletion_policy` and `external_id` ...\n\nIn the updated spec I also extended policy to include control of intrinsic function use in templates.",
      "parentUuid": "ce5d7208_7bded845",
      "revId": "51621215202706f44b633d938003ad02ea30f4ec",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
