      "writtenOn": "2026-06-04T12:52:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch, `OS::Nova::KeyPair` is potentially risky - the constructs are there for the zuul operator to block it via policy. And it **should be blocked** unless the users are trusted.\n\nI put in the following in the updated spec\u0027s Security section:\n\n\u003e The driver documentation will highlight resource types and \n\u003e intrinsic functions with security implications to help\n\u003e operators make informed decisions when configuring their\n\u003e allow-lists.  For example ``OS::Neutron::RBACPolicy``,\n\u003e ``OS::Nova::KeyPair``, ``yaql``, and ``make_url``.\n\nI also plan to change the examples in doc that use KeyPair for the ephemeral \"per-node\" keys, they can be passed directly via cloud_config instead of creating a keypair.",
      "parentUuid": "99d41729_1d2f762d",
      "revId": "51621215202706f44b633d938003ad02ea30f4ec",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    }
